    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d473">

                <pb facs="0900" n="840" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg840"/>

                <head>Mr. Hovey to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 107.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Lima, Peru,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-12-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 28, 1867.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Since my last dispatch No. 106, dated the
                    22d instant, no change of moment has taken place in the military situation
                    here.</p>
                <p>Colonel Prado has commenced the bombardment of Arequipa, but without, at latest
                    intelligence, having caused any great damage to life or property. A large
                    Blakely gun, while being conveyed to the camp of Colonel Prado, was spiked and
                    rendered useless by a detachment of the enemy’s forces.</p>
                <p>In the north the position is the same. The opposing forces were to have fought
                    the decisive engagement about the 23d or 24th of this month, but as yet we have
                    received no intelligence concerning the affair.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with great respect, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ALVIN P. HOVEY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
